# Shared-library exception types need default visibility on non-glibc Linux-like targets
id:                     E2182-draft-2301_80739235
trigger_tool:           cmake|clang|conan-create|ctest
phase:                  build|test|consumer-validation
error_signature:        "unsafe_wait.*catch|Subprocess aborted.*global_control|header.*Failed"
severity:               2
category:               abi|visibility|shared-library|platform-capability
match_keywords:         hidden exception RTTI, non-glibc Linux-like target, unsafe_wait visibility, shared library catch failure
root_cause:             A C++ exception class defined in a shared library can retain hidden visibility on a Linux-like target whose libc is not glibc. The producer and test executable then use different RTTI identities, so catches for the exception fail or the default assertion path aborts even though compilation and linking succeed.
affected_scope:         CMake shared-library builds using hidden default visibility on non-glibc Linux-like targets, especially tests that throw and catch exported exception classes.
verification_cmd:       Build the shared library and its test executable with hidden default visibility, run a throw/catch test across the shared-library boundary, and require the specific exception catch plus the complete remaining CTest inventory to pass.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           capability-scoped-exception-visibility
rec_description:        Preserve hidden visibility for ordinary symbols, but push default visibility around the exported exception type when the target's runtime/ABI capability requires it. Use a compiler/platform capability condition, not an application-level workaround or a blanket visibility change.
rec_command:            "patch the exception declaration; run patch-ng strict replay; run the affected throw/catch CTest cases"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               exported-exception-declaration
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      abi-symbol-readback
fallback_description:   If a target-specific visibility condition is uncertain, inspect the exported type and run a minimal cross-DSO throw/catch probe before changing the full test suite.
fallback_command:       "read exported exception symbol and execute a cross-DSO catch probe"
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          abi-validation
forbid_1_pattern:       "skip.*global_control|disable.*header.*test"
forbid_1_reason:        Removing the tests hides an ABI defect instead of fixing the exception identity.
forbid_1_consequence:   Consumers can still fail to catch library exceptions after a nominally successful build.
forbid_2_pattern:       "-fvisibility=default.*all"
forbid_2_reason:        A blanket visibility change expands the ABI surface and is unrelated to the narrow exception failure.
forbid_2_consequence:   Internal implementation symbols become exported without evidence that they are part of the public contract.
principles:             P007, P015
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
